  "branch": "fix/graph-frechet-mean-auto-selection-20261115",
  "title": "Select aligned Frechet means automatically for equipped graph spaces",
  "body": "## Problem\n\nThe graph branch in `FrechetMean(method=\"auto\")` assigns `AACFrechetMean` to the unused `method` local instead of the estimator factory. It therefore averages adjacency matrices without aligning their node labels. Equivalent relabelings can change the inferred graph mean, and AAC-specific options raise constructor errors.\n\n## Change\n\nSelect `AACFrechetMean` for graph spaces with an alignment structure. Graph spaces without an aligner continue to use their ordinary labeled-space mean, and an explicit `method=\"linear\"` still requests the arithmetic mean. The explicit AAC route is unchanged.\n\n## Validation\n\nThe same 12 new regression/control cases on unchanged base `2fc8e25eb8955767292552f9c0c1438be362ba8f` report **6 failures and 6 passes** on each backend. They fit real three-node undirected and four-node directed attributed graphs with independent node relabelings. Expected graph means are checked against an exhaustive NumPy permutation oracle, independent of the library aligner. Tests cover default/explicit auto, explicit AAC, labeled-graph means, caller input preservation, and AAC initialization/storage options.\n\nAt exact source `82f2541d9e306d8cb623190ee02b245d02fd3384`, all learning tests plus graph-space, Euclidean and matrix geometry tests report:\n\n- NumPy: **947 passed, 5 skipped, 414 deselected, 3 xfailed, 4 xpassed**.\n- Autograd: **949 passed, 3 skipped, 414 deselected, 2 xfailed, 5 xpassed**.\n- Ruff and applicable pre-commit hooks pass; source and diff checks pass.\n\n[Exact-source CI](https://github.com/Afloat16/geomstats/actions/runs/43674326692). Existing slow/redundant markers are excluded. Python 3.13.18 with the NumPy and Autograd backends; the full repository and PyTorch backend were not run.\n\n## Related work\n\nReviewed #2120, which introduced the factory branch, #1965's graph-space refactor, the AAC discussion in #2119, relevant all-state graph/mean history, and all six prior author PRs. Of 50 pre-existing fork heads, 17 contain the same unused-local assignment and 33 predate this factory; none contains this repair.\n",
  "validation_url": "https://github.com/Afloat16/geomstats/actions/runs/43674326692",
  "validation_commit": "ac612168bdc521e56c1f16095d3a97139d83f5ee",
